Commands
--------

api-key
~~~~~~~

api-key:generate
................

Generate a new valid API key

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:generate [-m|--name NAME] [-e|--expiration-date EXPIRATION-DATE] [-a|--author-only] [-d|--domain-only DOMAIN-ONLY] [-o|--no-orphan-visits]``

The api-key:generate generates a new valid API key.

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate

You can optionally set its name for tracking purposes with --name or -m:

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate --name Alice

You can optionally set its expiration date with --expiration-date or -e:

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:generate --expiration-date 2020-01-01

Options
^^^^^^^

\-\-name|-m
"""""""""""

The unique name by which this API key will be known

- **Accept value**: yes
- **Is value required**: yes
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``NULL``

\-\-expiration-date|-e
""""""""""""""""""""""

The date in which the API key should expire. Use any valid PHP format

- **Accept value**: yes
- **Is value required**: yes
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``NULL``

\-\-author-only|-a
""""""""""""""""""

Adds the "AUTHORED_SHORT_URLS" role to the new API key

- **Accept value**: no
- **Is value required**: no
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``false``

\-\-domain-only|-d
""""""""""""""""""

Adds the "DOMAIN_SPECIFIC" role to the new API key, with provided domain

- **Accept value**: yes
- **Is value required**: yes
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``NULL``

\-\-no-orphan-visits|-o
"""""""""""""""""""""""

Adds the "NO_ORPHAN_VISITS" role to the new API key

- **Accept value**: no
- **Is value required**: no
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``false``



api-key:disable
...............

Disables an API key by name

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:disable [<name>]``

The api-key:disable command allows you to disable an existing API key.

If no arguments are provided, you will be prompted to select one of the existing non-disabled API keys.

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:disable

You can optionally pass the API key name to be disabled:

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:disable the_key_name


Arguments
^^^^^^^^^

name

api-key:delete
..............

Deletes an API key by name

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:delete [<name>]``

The api-key:delete command allows you to delete an existing API key via its name.

If no arguments are provided, you will be prompted to select one of the existing API keys.

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:delete

You can optionally pass the API key name to be disabled:

    /usr/local/bin/shlink api-key:delete the_key_name


Arguments
^^^^^^^^^

name

api-key:list
............

Lists all the available API keys.

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:list [-e|--enabled-only]``

Lists all the available API keys.

Options
^^^^^^^

\-\-enabled-only|-e
"""""""""""""""""""

Tells if only enabled API keys should be returned.

- **Accept value**: no
- **Is value required**: no
- **Is multiple**: no
- **Is negatable**: no
- **Default**: ``false``



api-key:initial
...............

Tries to create initial API key

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:initial <api-key>``

Tries to create initial API key

Arguments
^^^^^^^^^

api-key

api-key:rename
..............

Renames an API key by name

Usage
^^^^^

- ``api-key:rename <old-name> <new-name>``

Renames an API key by name

Arguments
^^^^^^^^^

old-name

new-name

